# NOTE: '#' only starts a comment at the START of a line. A comment placed
# after a pattern becomes part of the pattern, so every note here is on its
# own line.

# ── macOS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ── Editor / tooling ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local dev-server config for the preview pane.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ── Working files that should not be served from GitHub Pages ────────────
# Briefs written for generating the artwork — useful locally, not part of
# the site.
ASSET-PROMPTS.md
Weichen-Fan-asset-brief.pdf
Weichen-Fan-asset-brief-2.pdf

# Lossless masters for the generated artwork. Each is several MB and only
# exists so a painting can be re-cropped or re-graded later; the site loads
# the WebP in assets/img/ instead.
assets/*-master.png

# ── Deliberately NOT ignored ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# assets/*.png and *.jpeg — the original full-size source images the site
#   was built from. Already in this repository's history, and the only
#   copies of the paper teasers and the organisation logos.
# scripts/ — install-portrait.sh is worth keeping.
